INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line monthly sales as a multiple of its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combos with their multiples and return rates, judge whether the spike is real demand or channel stuffing, and save a fully-sourced Markdown report to disk.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), unique regions, unique product lines, and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute 24-month baseline & anomaly multiples: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_sales / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/anomaly_multiples.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the anomaly_multiples.csv, select the top-3 (region, product_line, month) by highest multiple. For each, also retrieve the corresponding return_rate from the original CSV. Save a small summary CSV (top3_anomalies.csv) with columns: region, product_line, month, sales_volume, mean_24m, multiple, return_rate → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing signals: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute auxiliary signals from the CSV: (a) return_rate trend in the 3 months before/after the spike, (b) whether the spike is a single-month spike or sustained (compare month+1 sales to the spike month), (c) compare the spike month's return_rate to the 24-month average return_rate for that combo. Save a signals CSV (top3_signals.csv) → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded table: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) a data table showing the top-3 anomalies with region, product_line, month, sales, 24m mean, multiple, return_rate; (3) every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a conclusion paragraph judging whether each spike looks like real demand or channel stuffing, citing the auxiliary signals; (5) no external data, only from the local CSV → code_agent
